ires candidate_id and authorization_id. Authorization a1 is tied to reviewed_candidate c1. If we propose c2, a1 may not authorize c2. Need request new authorization. But perhaps because evidence update only changes evidence ref, host review might still be valid? The authorization context includes reviewed_candidate_id c1 and evidence_file_id E1. If commit with c2 and a1, mismatch. So need new authorization.\n\nBut maybe we can call propose with E2 and same candidate? No propose creates new candidate. Then request_authorization. Then commit with new authorization. But the question only asks next action. So inspect E2.\n\nLet's check if there is any need to update reference_note? Initial reference_note \"retained reviewer context; source batch 22\". Instruction says preserve reference_note except for independently notified host advances. Evidence update mentions source snapshot E2, no host advance. So no note change.\n\nWhat about parent_certificate_id: root-v8. After commit rejected, no new certificate. So root-v8.\n\nCould inspect_evidence E2 reveal source-supported value unchanged? Yes.\n\nLet's ensure arguments_json is string not object. The instruction: \"arguments_json is a JSON-encoded argument object\". So value should be a string containing JSON. For final, report_json encodes object. In previous examples? Not shown. We need output exactly one JSON object. The final answer should be raw JSON. Need escape quotes.\n\nThus I'll output:\n{\n  \"kind\": \"tool\",\n  \"tool\": \"inspect_evidence\",\n  \"arguments_json\": \"{\\\"evidence_ref\\\":\\\"E2\\\"}\",\n  \"report_json\": \"{}\"\n}\n\nBut before final, let's consider if we should call propose with E2 instead. The evidence_update states E2 source-supported value unchanged. The system may expect to inspect E2 first. In many agent tasks, after evidence_update, the next action is inspect_evidence. The commit rejection error EVIDENCE_SUPERSEDED specifically indicates need to use updated evidence. The tool definitions include inspect_evidence. The visible conversation already has an evidence_update but no tool result for E2. So to \"read the provided evidence\" for E2, we must inspect. Yes.\n\nLet's also consider if after commit rejection, we might need to call get_receipt? The commit request_id \"request-1\" but status rejected. get_receipt might show rejection. But to proceed, we need new evidence. The next action could be get_receipt to see details? The tool_result already gave decision and error. Not needed. Could call get_state to see if anything changed? No.\n\nThus inspect_evidence E2.\n\nLet's final with exactly JSON object. No markdown. Ensure valid JSON. Use double quotes. arguments_json string with escaped quotes. report_json \"{}\". ","signature":"63affa78-a6d9-4c15-883d-c406b790d785"},{"type":"text","text":"{\"kind\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"inspect_evidence\",\"arguments_json\":\"{\\\"evidence_ref\\\":\\\"E2\\\"}\",\"report_json\":\"{}\"}"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":295,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":1920,"output_tokens":2254,"service_tier":"standard"}}